.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/cross-spawn Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "cross-spawn"
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP

.PP
A cross platform solution to node's spawn and spawnSync\&.
.SH "Installation"
.PP
Node\&.js version 8 and up: \fR$ npm install cross-spawn\fP

.PP
Node\&.js version 7 and under: \fR$ npm install cross-spawn@6\fP
.SH "Why"
.PP
Node has issues when using spawn on Windows:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
It ignores \fRPATHEXT\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
It does not support \fRshebangs\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Has problems running commands with \fRspaces\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
Has problems running commands with posix relative paths (e\&.g\&.: \fR\&./my-folder/my-executable\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Has an \fRissue\fP with command shims (files in \fRnode_modules/\&.bin/\fP), where arguments with quotes and parenthesis would result in \fRinvalid syntax error\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
No \fRoptions\&.shell\fP support on node \fR<v4\&.8\fP
.PP

.PP
All these issues are handled correctly by \fRcross-spawn\fP\&. There are some known modules, such as \fRwin-spawn\fP, that try to solve this but they are either broken or provide faulty escaping of shell arguments\&.
.SH "Usage"
.PP
Exactly the same way as node's \fR\fRspawn\fP\fP or \fR\fRspawnSync\fP\fP, so it's a drop in replacement\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
const spawn = require('cross\-spawn');

// Spawn NPM asynchronously
const child = spawn('npm', ['list', '\-g', '\-depth', '0'], { stdio: 'inherit' });

// Spawn NPM synchronously
const result = spawn\&.sync('npm', ['list', '\-g', '\-depth', '0'], { stdio: 'inherit' });
.fi
.PP
.SH "Caveats"
.PP
.SS "Using \fRoptions\&.shell\fP as an alternative to \fRcross-spawn\fP"
Starting from node \fRv4\&.8\fP, \fRspawn\fP has a \fRshell\fP option that allows you run commands from within a shell\&. This new option solves the \fRPATHEXT\fP issue but:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
It's not supported in node \fR<v4\&.8\fP
.IP "\(bu" 2
You must manually escape the command and arguments which is very error prone, specially when passing user input
.IP "\(bu" 2
There are a lot of other unresolved issues from the \fBWhy\fP section that you must take into account
.PP

.PP
If you are using the \fRshell\fP option to spawn a command in a cross platform way, consider using \fRcross-spawn\fP instead\&. You have been warned\&.
.SS "\fRoptions\&.shell\fP support"
While \fRcross-spawn\fP adds support for \fRoptions\&.shell\fP in node \fR<v4\&.8\fP, all of its enhancements are disabled\&.

.PP
This mimics the Node\&.js behavior\&. More specifically, the command and its arguments will not be automatically escaped nor shebang support will be offered\&. This is by design because if you are using \fRoptions\&.shell\fP you are probably targeting a specific platform anyway and you don't want things to get into your way\&.
.SS "Shebangs support"
While \fRcross-spawn\fP handles shebangs on Windows, its support is limited\&. More specifically, it just supports \fR#!/usr/bin/env <program>\fP where \fR<program>\fP must not contain any arguments\&. 
.br
 If you would like to have the shebang support improved, feel free to contribute via a pull-request\&.

.PP
Remember to always test your code on Windows!
.SH "Tests"
.PP
\fR$ npm test\fP 
.br
 \fR$ npm test -- --watch\fP during development
